meta {
  name: Reject an unauthenticated migration run
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{adminUrl}}/migrations
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-api-key:
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 401
  res.body.error.code: eq UNAUTHORIZED
}

docs {
  The rest of /api/admin is unauthenticated because only the UI reaches it. This
  route rewrites stored data on demand, so it is guarded like the v1 surface —
  and the guard is worth a test precisely because nothing else in the folder
  would notice if it were dropped.
}
